### Step 3 – Pin visuals to a dashboard

#### What I did in Power BI Service
- Opened my report in the **PL300 – Practice Workspace**.
- Pinned a bar chart to a **new dashboard** named “Practice Dashboard”.
- Adjusted tile size and position.
- Pinned additional visuals (line chart, KPI) to the **existing dashboard**.
- Observed that tiles link back to the original report when clicked.
- Created a second dashboard to understand that a workspace can contain multiple dashboards.

#### What I learned
- Dashboards exist **only** in Power BI Service (not in Desktop).
- A dashboard is a **single-page layout** made of “tiles”.
- Pinning a visual creates a **tile** on a dashboard.
- A tile can be “live” or a snapshot depending on visual type.
- Dashboards can combine visuals from different reports and datasets.
- Clicking a tile takes you back to the source report.
- A workspace can contain many dashboards, but only one app.

